<% content_for :title, "ChatGPT access — Forge" %>

<div class="mx-auto w-full max-w-3xl">
  <header>
    <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-emerald-400">Account integration</p>
    <h1 class="mt-2 text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-zinc-50">ChatGPT access</h1>
    <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-zinc-400">Connect your existing Forge account to ChatGPT to manage articles, reviews and FAQs on websites assigned to you.</p>
  </header>

  <section class="<%= content_section_card_classes %> mt-6" aria-labelledby="mcp-setup-title">
    <h2 id="mcp-setup-title" class="text-lg font-semibold text-zinc-100">Connect in ChatGPT</h2>
    <ol class="mt-4 list-inside list-decimal space-y-2 text-sm leading-6 text-zinc-300">
      <li>Add a custom MCP server in ChatGPT and enter the server URL below.</li>
      <li>Sign in to Forge and approve the requested permissions.</li>
      <li>Ask ChatGPT to list your websites before creating content.</li>
    </ol>
    <div class="mt-5">
      <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-zinc-500">Server URL</p>
      <code class="mt-2 block overflow-x-auto rounded-lg border border-zinc-700 bg-zinc-950 px-3 py-3 text-sm text-emerald-300"><%= ENV.fetch("MCP_RESOURCE_URL", "https://forge.1344.fr/mcp") %></code>
    </div>
    <div class="mt-5">
      <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-zinc-500">Suggested plugin description</p>
      <p class="mt-2 rounded-lg border border-zinc-800 bg-zinc-950/70 px-3 py-3 text-sm text-zinc-300">Manage articles, reviews and FAQs for websites assigned to your Forge account. Changes require your approval in Forge before they are saved or published.</p>
    </div>
    <p class="mt-5 text-xs leading-5 text-zinc-500">ChatGPT generates the text. Creating, editing, deleting or publishing content prepares a proposal; you review and approve each proposal in Forge. New content starts as a draft. Publishing requires a separate approval.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="mt-8" aria-labelledby="mcp-connections-title">
    <h2 id="mcp-connections-title" class="text-lg font-semibold text-zinc-100">Authorized connections</h2>
    <% if @tokens.empty? %>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-zinc-400">No ChatGPT connection is currently authorized.</p>
    <% else %>
      <ul class="mt-4 divide-y divide-zinc-800 rounded-xl border border-zinc-800 bg-zinc-900/50 px-4 sm:px-6">
        <% @tokens.each do |token| %>
          <li class="flex flex-col gap-3 py-4 sm:flex-row sm:items-center sm:justify-between">
            <div class="min-w-0">
              <p class="break-words text-sm font-medium text-zinc-100"><%= token.application&.name || "ChatGPT MCP client" %></p>
              <p class="mt-1 text-xs text-zinc-400">Authorized <%= l(token.created_at, format: :long) %> · <%= token.scopes.to_a.join(", ") %></p>
            </div>
            <%= button_to "Revoke", mcp_authorization_path(token), method: :delete, form: { data: { turbo_confirm: "Revoke this ChatGPT connection?" } }, class: danger_button_classes %>
          </li>
        <% end %>
      </ul>
    <% end %>
  </section>
</div>
